# ask-this-book

Read `GOAL.md` first (the goal + constitution — the only thing that can block
work), then `AGENTS.md` at the repo root: hard rules, current phase state,
machine facts, and verify commands. `BUILD_PLAN.md` is the living plan
(tactics that expire; renamed from `README.md`); `README.md` is the human-facing
overview; `GLOSSARY.md` translates the repo's vocabulary (sealed suite, gate,
capture, retry, ...) into plain words when a term is unclear.

## Artifacts

- Never write an artifact to the repo root or to a new flat path under
  `artifacts/`; only `prune.py` and `README.md` sit at its top level.
- Consult the decision list in `artifacts/README.md` before creating anything.
- Every artifact carries its date: `family-YYYY-MM-DD[-label].ext`.
- A run is promoted into `artifacts/` only when a doc or commit names it;
  otherwise it stays in `artifacts/runs/` or `artifacts/scratch/`.
